This framework using Proxy Pattern Structural Patterns – Deal with how classes and objects are composed/connected:
Which have 3 main components: Subject (Interface) RealObject and Proxy

✔ Load only when needed (lazy loading)
✔ Load only once (caching)
✔ Avoid heavy operations (disk I/O, network, CPU)
✔ Control access to the real object

=> Proxy controls access and adds behavior around a real object(it's supposed to do only ONE job (displaying) — not connection logic), 
while keeping client code unchanged and keeping the real object focused only on its main job.
